        "created_at": "2013-04-10T00:58:55.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p><a href=\"http://www.gaminghoopla.com/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">http://www.gaminghoopla.com/</a></p><p><span>A friend of mine just asked me if I wanted to join him for this the other day, so I couldn't register as a judge (or see if a &gt;G rep wanted to make the trip and do so), but there's a charity gaming event in Janesville, WI (between Madison, WI and Rockford, IL) the weekend of 4/19-4/21. There's a registration fee and a bunch of raffles, I believe, with all the proceeds going to someone's Relay for Life team, which supports the American Cancer Society.</span></p><p><span>I'll be there on Saturday with a buddy, and while they have a schedule of all the games they're hosting, there will apparently be a bunch of open tables for playing other games, and the website says they'll have the full GenCon game library. I'm going to bring my sleeved copy of Sentinels + Rook City in case their copy is in use, and hopefully I'll spread the good news of SotM to the gamers of South Central (Wisconsin).</span></p><p><span>If anyone is local and wants to meet there, or if someone's in the Milwaukee area and wants to carpool, it looks like a fun event for a good cause. I think my friend went last year and said it was fun... they have a game exchange, a couple tournaments set up, and I think I saw an event for guidance with using Kickstarter to fund your game. (I, for one, think it would be&nbsp;<em>hilarious</em> if a &gt;G rep showed up and sat in on the Kickstarter event.) Check out the schedule to see if anything tickles your fancy; we registered for the afternoon session of one game but plan on floating the rest of the time (and yes, definitely playing SotM).</span></p>",
